## Voices and input

{% if capabilities.voice_mode | default("preset_catalog") == "preset_catalog" -%}
This package exposes {{ capabilities.voice_count }} preset speaker IDs,
`{{ capabilities.voice_ids }}`. It produces {{ capabilities.sample_rate_hz }} Hz
mono F32 audio. No default speaker is invented; every request must select a
Voice.
{%- elif capabilities.voice_mode | default("preset_catalog") == "fixed_default" -%}
This package has one fixed package-default Voice and does not expose a preset
speaker catalog. It produces {{ capabilities.sample_rate_hz }} Hz mono F32
audio. Callers omit Voice selection; the package always uses its trained Voice.
{%- else -%}
This package exposes no preset speaker catalog. Its package default has no
fixed identity and no speaker conditioning: with no Voice Profile supplied,
which speaker a request produces is emergent, and the synthesis seed alone does
not pin it. Reproducing a speaker needs the same seed **and** the same
Execution Backend, package, and decode settings; switching between the CPU and
CUDA backends can produce a different speaker for an otherwise identical
request.
{%- if capabilities.speaker_backend_variation | default("") %} Measured on this
package's own validation cases,
{{- " " }}{{ capabilities.speaker_backend_variation }}.
{%- endif %} Callers who want a stable identity should instead build a Voice
Profile from
{%- if "reference_audio" in capabilities.voice_profile_sources and "description_text" in capabilities.voice_profile_sources %} Reference Audio (voice cloning) or Description Text (voice design)
{%- elif "reference_audio" in capabilities.voice_profile_sources %} Reference Audio (voice cloning)
{%- elif "description_text" in capabilities.voice_profile_sources %} Description Text (voice design)
{%- endif %} and pass it to the request. It produces {{ capabilities.sample_rate_hz }} Hz mono F32 audio.
{%- endif %}

{% if "text_utf8" in capabilities.input_kinds -%}
This package accepts raw UTF-8 text through the built-in
`{{ capabilities.frontend_provider }}` frontend{% if "token_ids" in capabilities.input_kinds %}, and also accepts exact token
IDs already produced by the same vocabulary{% endif %}. The frontend tokenizes text
directly: no grapheme-to-phoneme conversion happens or is needed, and the
runtime does not silently invoke eSpeak or download a frontend.
{%- else -%}
This package accepts UTF-8 phoneme strings through the built-in
`{{ capabilities.frontend_provider }}` frontend{% if "token_ids" in capabilities.input_kinds %}, and also accepts exact token IDs{% endif %}. The frontend
validates UTF-8, maps each Unicode scalar through the symbol table embedded in
the GGUF, and applies the model's blank-insertion rule.

The built-in frontend does not perform grapheme-to-phoneme conversion or text
normalization. Callers starting from raw text must currently run a compatible
G2P frontend externally. The runtime does not silently invoke eSpeak or download
a frontend.
{%- endif %}

## Usage

Build synthesize.cpp and synthesize a deterministic request:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/handy-computer/synthesize.cpp.git
cd synthesize.cpp
cmake -S . -B build -DSYNTH_BUILD_CLI=ON
cmake --build build -j

hf download {{ target_repo }} {{ model_slug }}-{{ usage.profile }}.gguf{% for sidecar in sidecars | default([]) %} {{ sidecar.filename }}{% endfor %} \
  --local-dir models/{{ model_slug }}

build/bin/synthesize-cli \
  --model models/{{ model_slug }}/{{ model_slug }}-{{ usage.profile }}.gguf \
  --output output.wav \
{% if "text_utf8" in capabilities.input_kinds %}  --text "{{ usage.text }}" \
{% else %}  --phonemes "{{ usage.phonemes }}" \
{% endif %}  --language {{ languages[0] }} \
{% if capabilities.voice_mode | default("preset_catalog") == "preset_catalog" %}  --voice {{ usage.voice }} \
{% endif %}  --seed 0
```

The same local GGUF can be loaded through the public C ABI and wrapped by C++,
Rust, or Python. Model loading never contacts Hugging Face.

